Description: Put the title-bar button click areas where the buttons are drawn
 With a Marco theme the decorator shifted the click area of every right-hand
 button left and down by the width of the invisible resize border (10 px), so
 the upper and right parts of minimize, maximize and close did not respond.
 The geometry returned by libmarco already includes that border.
Author: Spaced Linux Developers <dev@spacedlinux.com>
Bug: https://github.com/crhy/spaced/issues/279
Forwarded: no
---
--- a/gtk-window-decorator/gtk-window-decorator.c
+++ b/gtk-window-decorator/gtk-window-decorator.c
@@ -3428,17 +3428,13 @@
     *y = space->clickable.y;
     *w = space->clickable.width;
     *h = space->clickable.height;
-#ifdef HAVE_MARCO_1_22_2
-    /*compensate for offset caused by invisible borders
-     *taken straight from compiz 0.9
-     *but exclude left side buttons so resize border isn't blocked
+    /* The clickable rectangle is already in frame coordinates, and the frame
+     * the button windows live in includes Marco's invisible resize border
+     * (see the frame extents in update_window_decoration_...).  An extra
+     * "compensation" here moved every right-hand button's click area left by
+     * the invisible border and DOWN by it, away from the drawn button, so only
+     * the lower-left part of each button responded.
      */
-    if (*x >= 20)
-    {
-        *x = *x - fgeom.borders.invisible.left;
-        *y = *y + fgeom.borders.invisible.top;
-    }
-#endif
     return TRUE;
 }
 
